WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:02.050
The partnership works as a connected system Daniel’s diary work affects decisions, documents and other people’s accepted assignments. These interfaces are connected responsibilities, not a universal hierarchy. Each person or function makes a different contribution. Select a card to hear a full explanation, then consider how a missing decision or unaccepted assignment would affect the others. Request → identify the required owners → obtain the separate decisions/acceptance → update the controlled record → check completion evidence. Example dependency : a business preference for a physical lunch does not by itself establish protective input, transport arrangements or accepted monitoring. Existing afternoon arrangements do not automatically cover the proposed lunch. Workbook: §§1.1.3, 1.5, 1.7.3 and 1.8. No extra command powers or guaranteed services are introduced.
